      "id": "ray-diagram",
      "label": "Equal steps: H → lower; L → upper",
      "description": "Use the corrected proof’s discipline: preserve equal relations rather than trust a sketch. Assume a straight light path in uniform air. Along one straight line, equal horizontal runs have equal vertical changes. H→O drops one unit; the equally long run beyond O drops one more, reaching the lower screen mark (−1). L→O rises one unit; continuing equally far rises one more, reaching the upper mark (+1). Thus H→lower and L→upper. The earlier equality reasoning helps work out this consequence; the old triangle proof does not establish the physical straight-path assumption. A ray is a drawn path, not a luminous thread.",
