      "description": "Insert the supplied lunar radius and period into the circular construction: 2π² × 382,200,000 m × (1 s / 2,358,720 s)² ≈ 0.001356 m, or 1.36 mm of inward departure in 1 s. Separately, r ≈ 60R makes the candidate ratio 1/60² = 1/3600. The terrestrial branch must now supply the surface fall for comparison. This is one Moon-distance check, not a claim to have tested several planetary orbits.",
