      "b": "cross-orbit-check",
      "out": "shared-motion-account",
      "description": "Scale the terrestrial displacement by the candidate inverse-square ratio: 4.90 m ÷ 60² = 0.001361… m ≈ 1.36 mm in 1 s. The separate orbit calculation gave 0.001356… m ≈ 1.36 mm in 1 s: agreement at the stated rounding, not exact equality. Equivalently, 9.80 m/s² ÷ 3600 ≈ 0.00272 m/s². Keeping surface acceleration unchanged at the lunar distance would instead predict 4.90 m in 1 s, about 3600 times too much. This comparison supports one quantitative account of the two motions under the stated idealizations.",
