      "description": "Factor the repeated inhibit: (A AND NOT C) OR (B AND NOT C) = (A OR B) AND NOT C. The factored model has A and B in parallel, with one shared NOT C contact in series with that pair: three contacts rather than four, saving one. For ABC=000,001,010,011,100,101,110,111, both models give Y=0,0,1,0,1,0,1,0. Equivalence means the same eight ideal, static outputs. It does not imply equal fault tolerance: if the shared NOT C sticks closed, C no longer inhibits either request; a stuck-closed C contact in the four-contact model bypasses the inhibit on its own branch. No reliability, timing, or total-cost claim follows from the contact saving.",
