      "a": "rule-proposal",
      "b": "checked-logic",
      "out": "explicit-allocation",
      "description": "Reuse the checked logic method to test the draft’s cases, not to choose whose needs matter. Let W be measured nonnegative inlet m³ for one day. If W < 8: U=W, D=0. If 8 ≤ W < 12: U=8, D=W−8. If W ≥ 12: U=8, D=4; W−12 passes onward. The branches do not overlap: W=8 gives U8/D0, not U8/D4; W=12 gives U8/D4. Thus dry W=6 gives U6/D0. A consistent priority rule can still leave a justified complaint.",
