      "out": "revisable-agreement",
      "description": "U and D adopt a replacement for this trial: with measured W ≥ 12, deliver U8/D4 and pass the excess onward; with 0 ≤ W < 12, deliver U=(2/3)W and D=(1/3)W. Dry6 now gives U4/D2: each receives half its stated need, and shortfalls U4/D2 still total 6. The original U6/D0 and both needs remain in the record. A jointly accountable gatekeeper implements and records the new releases; either group may contest them through review. Missing readings, changed needs or delivery losses require renewed review. This is an adopted local ration, not proof of a uniquely best or fully sufficient allocation. Later cases inherit the practice of checking and revising their current agreement, not Alder’s numeric shares.",
